-0.03 -0.
// generated by: flint, validated by: [mpmath, decimal] ; near-zero half-ULP tie: x = +/-10^-(S/2) puts the second-order term of expm1(x) = x + x^2/2 + x^3/6 + ... at EXACTLY half an ULP past the grid point x at scale S (x^2/2 = (1/2)*10^-S), so the round is decided only by x^3/6 at depth 3S/2+1 - S/2 digits below the kernel's SCALE+GUARD, forcing the Ziv escalation. A kernel that stops at the guard sees ...5000 and applies the exact-tie rule, which is wrong in a different mode per sign: HalfToEven mis-rounds the positive row (last digit even, so the tie rule holds it down), HalfTowardZero the negative one. Series arm - |x| <= 1 at every cell, so these rows are evidence about expm1_series, not expm1_via_exp. One pair per even golden scale S <= 820, above which the deciding term falls past the oracle's stored 1233 digits and the value would read as a tie it is not
-0.1 -0.
// generated by: flint, validated by: [mpmath, decimal] ; policy arm boundary: src/policy/expm1.rs classify routes |x| <= 1 in RAW storage units (raw <= 10^SCALE) to the Series kernel and everything else to ViaExp - an analytic validity wall, not a tuning knob: outside it the series carries no range reduction and either alternates into cancellation (x < 0) or peaks at e^x/sqrt(2*pi*x) (x > 0), and it stops at SERIES_CAP, returning a TRUNCATED value rather than a slow one. These are the last Series-routed and the first ViaExp-routed arguments at each scale - 1 -/+ 10^-S and -1 +/- 10^-S, one ULP either side of the wall on both signs, plus the exact +/-1 that the <= keeps on the Series side. An off-by-one in that raw comparison hands an argument to a kernel that is not valid for it, and only an input adjacent to the wall can see it. These carry no sub-ULP tie structure of their own, but the gen_precision wall still reaches them at the deepest scale, where a value whose two guard digits both happen to be zero reads as exact. A row is graded at EVERY cell whose envelope holds it, not only the one it was derived for, so the binding constraint is that the first deciding digit BELOW the LSB must fall inside the 1233 stored digits at every such cell - at a far deeper scale that is a much later series term. Inputs failing that anywhere were dropped; what remains is decidable at every cell it reaches
