// generated by: flint, validated by: [mpmath, decimal] ; exact point and sign change: expm1(0) = 0 is the ONLY exact value on the whole domain - e^a is transcendental for every rational a != 0 (Lindemann-Weierstrass), so expm1 is irrational at every other input the golden set can hold, which is why oracle/exactness.py classifies it in the pure-transcendental family. Every rounding mode must return an exact zero here with no directed-mode step. +/-2 are the nearest plain ViaExp anchors either side of the wall - a sign-symmetric pair outside the Series region without being a boundary case itself
-2 -0.
// generated by: flint, validated by: [mpmath, decimal] ; exact point and sign change: expm1(0) = 0 is the ONLY exact value on the whole domain - e^a is transcendental for every rational a != 0 (Lindemann-Weierstrass), so expm1 is irrational at every other input the golden set can hold, which is why oracle/exactness.py classifies it in the pure-transcendental family. Every rounding mode must return an exact zero here with no directed-mode step. +/-2 are the nearest plain ViaExp anchors either side of the wall - a sign-symmetric pair outside the Series region without being a boundary case itself
0 0
// generated by: flint, validated by: [mpmath, decimal] ; directed-mode guard step, positive half: x = +10^-m gives expm1(x) = 10^-m + (1/2)*10^-2m, one ULP plus a hair above zero at S = m, with the deciding residual at depth 2m+1 - roughly m digits below the kernel's SCALE+GUARD. A kernel that stops at the guard sees ...000, concludes the result is EXACT, and returns the nearest-mode answer under Ceiling, which must instead step 10^-m up to 2*10^-m. Same shape as the ln defect in #73 (Ceiling returning the HalfToEven answer near 1): the input steps AROUND the guard rather than stressing what the guard already covers. Bounded to m <= 616, and the bound is REAL here where it is not for the negative mirror above - 10^-m + (1/2)*10^-2m is an ADDITION, so once 2m+1 > 1233 the stored value truncates to a clean power of ten and reads as exact, whereas the negative form's SUBTRACTION borrows and leaves a 9-run immediately below the LSB that stays visible at every scale. The six deepest golden scales (693, 900, 923, 924, 1200, 1231) therefore carry no positive row and are covered by the negative mirror alone
0. 0.
